  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Democratic Partnership Challenge-Task Force Tunisia</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SK">ZPC zamestnancov MZV a EZ SR do Tuniska v r&#xe1;mci iniciat&#xed;vy &#x201e;Democratic Partnership Challenge-Task Force Tunisia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="SK">&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot; align=&quot;justify&quot;&gt;V&#xa0;r&#xe1;mci iniciat&#xed;vy &#x201e;Democratic Partnership Challenge&#x201c; pod hlavi&#x10d;kou Spolo&#x10d;enstva demokraci&#xed; (SD) zameranej na pomoc pri prechode k&#xa0;demokracii Slovensko spolu s&#xa0;Holandskom spolupredsedalo Task Force Tunisia v roku 2013.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot; align=&quot;justify&quot;&gt;Z&#xe1;merom tejto aktivity s&#xa0;p&#xf4;vodne pl&#xe1;novanou d&#x13a;&#x17e;kou trvania 2 roky (pred&#x13a;&#x17e;enou o&#xa0;6 mesiacov &#x2013; do konca r. 2013)&#xa0;bolo&lt;b&gt; pom&#xf4;c&#x165; Tunisku s&#xa0;prechodn&#xfd;m obdob&#xed;m, prispie&#x165; k&#xa0;formovaniu Tuniska ako &#xfa;spe&#x161;n&#xe9;ho pr&#xed;behu zmien v&#xa0;regi&#xf3;ne severnej Afriky.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot; align=&quot;justify&quot;&gt;Tunisko po obdob&#xed; autoritat&#xed;vnej vl&#xe1;dy sa sna&#x17e;&#xed; uskuto&#x10d;ni&#x165; demokratick&#xe9; zmeny a&#xa0;predlo&#x17e;ilo zoznam oblast&#xed;, v&#xa0;ktor&#xfd;ch vid&#xed; priority reforiem: &lt;b&gt;(a)&lt;/b&gt; reforma bezpe&#x10d;nostn&#xe9;ho sektora, &lt;b&gt;(b)&lt;/b&gt; reforma s&#xfa;dnictva, &lt;b&gt;(c)&lt;/b&gt; reforma verejnej spr&#xe1;vy, &lt;b&gt;(d)&lt;/b&gt; podpora region&#xe1;lneho rozvoja a&#xa0;&lt;b&gt;(e)&lt;/b&gt; budovanie ob&#x10d;ianskej spolo&#x10d;nosti.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;As part of the &quot;Democratic Partnership Challenge&quot; under the auspices of the Community of Democracies (CD) aimed to assist the transition to democracy Slovakia and the Netherlands co-chaired the Task Force Tunisia. The aim of this activity was to help Tunisia with the transitional period to contribute to the shaping of Tunisia as a success story of changes in the region of North Africa. Tunisia after a period of authoritarian government has been&#xa0;trying to introduce democratic change and provided a list of areas in which sees its reform priorities: (a) security sector reform, (b) judicial reform, (c) public administration reform, (d) promoting regional development and (e ) the development of civil society.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
